id: pm-gh1609
title: "GH-1609: investigate dead-writer recovery after a process is killed inside a commit fence"
description: "New GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1609 compares Linux Node24.19.0 plain non-Git tracker behavior: a strace-injected SIGKILL at the first rename, followed by another writer, reportedly succeeds4/4 on2026.10.21 but fails3/4 on2026.10.26 with lock_conflict and owner process dead after roughly3seconds. The report dates the change to2026.10.23 commit fencing and describes a separate frozen-clock downstream timeout. Reproduce independently and compare the owner-death reclaim and commit-fence cleanup gates, preserving live/unknown owner and stale-writer safety. Do not infer a root cause or bypass fences from the report alone."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
